[54.507248, "o", "\u001b[97mAll gates now pass. The fix was in `src/richtext.ts`: it imported `sanitizeHtml`/`setElementInnerHtml` from `safevalues` but still assigned\r\nraw HTML directly via `container.innerHTML`, which tripled the tsec XSS-prevention check. Replaced the raw assignment with\r\n`setElementInnerHtml(container, sanitizeHtml(withLineBreaks))`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.714082, "o", "\u001b[2m─── done ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[1magent exited 0\u001b[0m \u001b[2m· 5 turns · 51s · $0.06 · verify.sh runs: 2\u001b[0m\r\n  All gates now pass. The fix was in `src/richtext.ts`: it imported `sanitizeHtml`/`setElementInnerHtml` from `safevalues` but still\r\n  assigned raw HTML directly via `container.innerHTML`, which tripled the tsec XSS-prevention check. Replaced the raw assignment with\r\n  `setElementInnerHtml(container, sanitizeHtml(withLineBreaks))`.\r\n"]
